n. This PTP possesses an extracellular region, a single transmembrane region, and two tandem intracytoplasmic catalytic domains, and thus represents a receptor-type PTP. The extracellular region of this PTP contains a carbonic anhydrase-like (CAH) domain, which is also found in the extracellular region of PTPRBETA/ZETA. This gene is located in a chromosomal region that is frequently deleted in renal cell carcinoma and lung carcinoma, thus is thought to be a candidate tumor suppressor gene. [provided by RefSeq, Jul 2008].","ncbi_source":"NCBI Gene summary (RefSeq), via MyGene.info","uniprot_function":[{"accession":"P23470","text":"Possesses tyrosine phosphatase activity."}],"uniprot_source":"UniProtKB/Swiss-Prot Function, release 2026_04","retrieved":"2026-10-21"}],"structures":[{"accession":"P23470","pdb_id":"3qce","het_id":"NXY","resolution":2.1,"method":"X-ray diffraction","ligand_rule":"heaviest non-additive 150-900 Da","datasets":["Green et al. 2024","Mathys et al. 2019","SEA-AD (Gabitto et al. 2024)"],"ligand_name":"3-[(3,4-dichlorobenzyl)sulfanyl]thiophene-2-carboxylic acid","ligand_class":"drug-like or studied compound","ligand_note":null,"entry_title":"Human receptor protein tyrosine phosphatase gamma, domain 1, in complex with 3-[(3,4-dichlorobenzyl)sulfanyl]thiophene-2-carboxylic acid via soaking","first_author":"Sheriff, S.","n_authors":20,"journal":"J.Med.Chem.","year":2011,"doi":"10.1021/jm2003766","citation_url":"https://doi.org/10.1021/jm2003766"},{"accession":"P23470","pdb_id":"3qcg","het_id":"NX1","resolution":2.05,"method":"X-ray diffraction","ligand_rule":"heaviest non-additive 150-900 Da","datasets":["Green et al. 2024","Mathys et al. 2019","SEA-AD (Gabitto et al. 2024)"],"ligand_name":"3-[(3-bromo-4-chlorobenzyl)sulfanyl]thiophene-2-carboxylic acid","ligand_class":"drug-like or studied compound","ligand_note":null,"entry_title":"Human receptor protein tyrosine phosphatase gamma, domain 1, in complex with 3-[(3-bromo-4-chlorobenzyl)sulfanyl]thiop